WEBVTT

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:06.280
Knitting a sideways V-neck opening is a
matter of understanding short row

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.520
increases and short row decreases.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.280
Using short rows avoids
a stair-step V-neck edge.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.080
Now be sure to practice this first.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:19.560
You'll end with the carriage on the left.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.640
It's okay to knit an
extra row if you need to.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:27.760
Start the short row decreases on the
right-hand side of your knitting.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:29.320
Opposite the carriage.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:31.840
Set your carriage to hold.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:34.800
Put the needles in hold as
instructed in the pattern.

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:36.800
And don't forget to wrap.

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:16.335
When the first side of the V is complete,
knit 1 row from left to

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:18.160
right across all the needles.

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:21.720
This will enclose the wraps,
making it easier to bind

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:23.120
off those neckline stitches.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.800
Next, bind off those neckline stitches.

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:37.360
You're halfway there.

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:47.120
The working yarn is now on the right side
of the needles and work,

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:48.680
and carriage is on the right.

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:53.680
Hang a cast-on rag over the needles
for the second side of the V.

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.880
Knit 1 row of ravel cord.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:07.280
Using the working yarn,
cast on with a method of your choice

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:09.320
over those new neckline stitches.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:11.560
Make sure it's a closed cast-on.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:15.240
An e-wrap or a crochet cast-on will work.

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:18.120
Your carriage is on the right.

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:22.600
Knit across all the needles to
position the carriage on the left.

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:27.840
And you'll begin the short row
increases at the point of the V.

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:32.680
Put the neckline needles
into hold position.

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:36.855
Set your carriage to hold
and put the first set of shaping

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:38.440
needles into working position.

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:40.880
Knit across and wrap.

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:51.240
Continue the short row shaping until
all the needles are back into work.

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:03.375
When all of the needles are back into work
and you've finished the second side of

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:06.320
the V, knit across all of the needles.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.560
And continue knitting the
shoulder of the sweater.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:21.640
When you're ready, remove the
cast-on rag and block that neckline.

